C.1.6 Information
Information giving requirements for installation, maintenance, charging and handling shall be included in the battery and/or truck instruction handbook.
The instruction handbook shall contain information about the charging areas and their ventilation and all the necessary safety measures to be taken to minimize the risk of burn from electrolyte contact to skin and eyes according to EN 62485-3:2014, Clause 7.
NOTE During battery charging gases are evolved from all secondary cells and batteries using aqueous electrolytes. When emitted into the ambient atmosphere an explosive mixture will be created if the hydrogen concentration exceeds 4 % hydrogen by volume in air (LEL, lower explosion limit).

Battery compartment and electrical enclosures for trucks with nominal voltages greater than 60 V DC shall bear a durable warning sign conforming to EN 60204-1:2006, 16.2.
Each traction battery container shall be marked legibly and indelibly with the following information:
� name and address of battery manufacturer;
� type;
� serial number;
� nominal battery voltage (within one container);
� capacity in ampere hours at the five-hour rate;
� service mass (with ballast if used to compensate for lack of battery mass);
� mandatory relevant marking12;
� symbols to inform and warn the personnel of risks associated with batteries and battery installations according to EN 62485-3:2014, 11.1.

A.4.8 Dielectric test
Each connector without cables shall be able to withstand, for 1 min, an alternating current, with a frequency from 25 Hz up to 100 Hz and an effective voltage of 2 000 V applied:
� between the main contacts;
