A.4.5 Temperature rise test
Connectors shall be subjected to a temperature rise test.
Test samples shall be connected to cables with cross-section specified in Table A.1. Cables shall be connected by one of the methods recommended by the connector manufacturer. Each connector cable shall have a length of 2 m.
Tests shall be carried out under rated current as defined in Table A.1 and at an ambient temperature of (25 � 5) �C;

The test shall be carried out until temperatures are stable within a deviation margin of 2 �C over a period of 30 min;
The rise in temperature shall be measured with thermocouples or by other methods of equivalent precision at the highest temperature point of the connector;
Temperature rise shall not exceed 65 K in relation to the ambient temperature of (25 � 5) �C.

A.6 Information for use
All connectors shall bear legibly and indelibly, the following information:
a) name of manufacturer or trademark;
b) nominal voltage;
c) maximum voltage;
d) rated current in ampere; and
e) the symbols '+' and '-' corresponding to the contacts to be connected with the positive and negative poles of the battery;
f) alphanumeric identification of the auxiliary contacts shall be provided.
NOTE Information in b) can also be conveyed by the coding device.

